### Checks

- [x] I have checked that this issue has not already been reported.
- [x] I have confirmed this bug exists on the [latest version](https://crates.io/crates/polars) of Polars.

### Reproducible example

`crates/polars-ooc/examples/drift.rs` — installs polars-ooc's own global
allocator, then allocates on threads that immediately exit while the **main**
thread owns and frees the memory. A ~320 MB anchor is held alive for the whole
run, so true usage never drops. `main` and `fresh` do identical work; only the
lifetime of the allocating thread differs.

```rust
use std::sync::mpsc;

#[global_allocator]
static A: polars_ooc::Allocator = polars_ooc::Allocator;

fn est() -> u64 { polars_ooc::estimate_memory_usage() }

fn cycle(rounds: usize, per_thread: usize, block: usize, fresh_thread: bool) {
    for _ in 0..rounds {
        if fresh_thread {
            let (tx, rx) = mpsc::channel::<Vec<Vec<u8>>>();
            let h = std::thread::spawn(move || {
                let mut v = Vec::with_capacity(per_thread);
                for _ in 0..per_thread { v.push(vec![7u8; block]); }
                tx.send(v).unwrap();
            });
            let owned = rx.recv().unwrap();
            h.join().unwrap();  // thread is now dead; its residual drift is gone
            drop(owned);        // the main thread pays the -dealloc
        } else {
            let mut v = Vec::with_capacity(per_thread);
            for _ in 0..per_thread { v.push(vec![7u8; block]); }
            drop(v);
        }
    }
}

fn main() {
    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();
    let regime = args.get(1).map(|s| s.as_str()).unwrap_or("fresh");
    let rounds: usize = args.get(2).and_then(|s| s.parse().ok()).unwrap_or(700);
    let per_thread: usize = args.get(3).and_then(|s| s.parse().ok()).unwrap_or(8);
    let block: usize = args.get(4).and_then(|s| s.parse().ok()).unwrap_or(64 * 1024);

    // polars-config is a LazyLock otherwise only touched by the engine
    let _ = polars_config::config();

    // anchor: alive for the whole run, so true usage never falls below this
    let anchor: Vec<Vec<u8>> = (0..320).map(|_| vec![3u8; 1024 * 1024]).collect();
    let anchor_bytes: usize = anchor.iter().map(|b| b.len()).sum();

    let budget = polars_config::config().ooc_memory_budget_bytes();
    // mirrors MemoryManager::should_spill() (memory_manager.rs:61-67) with no
    // spill/prefetch in progress, which is the state at the start of a query
    let would_spill = |usage: u64| usage > budget;

    let base = est();
    println!("anchor_bytes={anchor_bytes} threshold={} budget_bytes={budget}",
             polars_config::get_ooc_drift_threshold());
    println!("base_estimate={base} would_spill={}", would_spill(base));

    let quarter = rounds / 4;
    for q in 1..=4 {
        cycle(quarter, per_thread, block, regime == "fresh");
        println!("after_round_{}={}", q * quarter, est());
    }

    let fin = est();
    let checksum: u64 = anchor.iter().map(|b| b[0] as u64).sum();
    assert_eq!(checksum, 320 * 3);   // the anchor is provably still alive
    println!("final_estimate={fin} would_spill={}", would_spill(fin));
    drop(anchor);
}
```

Run:

```
cargo build --release -p polars-ooc --example drift --no-default-features
POLARS_OOC_MEMORY_BUDGET_MB=256 ./target/release/examples/drift main  700 8 65536
POLARS_OOC_MEMORY_BUDGET_MB=256 ./target/release/examples/drift fresh 700 8 65536
```

