{"repository": "pola-rs/polars", "task_candidate_id": 19175, "repository_id": 207, "issue_number": 29973, "github_issue_id": 5863822770, "html_url": "https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/issues/29973", "created_at": "2026-10-15T09:44:56+00:00", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "title": "Generalization of limit pushdown into slice pushdown and into simple filter pushdown", "body_text": "### Description

I would like Polars to have better support of slice pushdown. Currently, the codebase usually handles only a weaker version of this, which is "head" pushdown. For example, in IO plugins, you get a limit keyword indicating the number of rows (see #23026), in `LazyFrameResolver` you also get `limit`., etc. Generally, there's no good support for "tail" pushdown, or more generally, slice pushdown. I would like to translate all the support for limit pushdown support into slice pushdown support, and the IO sources or operators that can only support head pushdown would apply only that part.

Furthermore, slice pushdown is just a filter. A filter on a hidden column that is the row index. A column which can be deterministic (if order is maintained) or non-deterministic. By treating it differently from a filter, we run into issues like #22790, where it is necessary to run slice pushdown, then filter pushdown, then slice pushdown. And the API also needs to pass it separately from the rest of filters. An additional improvement would be to incorporate the slice pushdown into the filters. (I'm not sure how to properly do this, given that the index column has no name and giving it a name could make it class with user names.)", "labels_json": "["enhancement"]", "state": "open", "assignment_state": "unassigned", "is_locked": 0, "has_linked_open_pr": 0, "comment_count": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-10-15T09:50:49+00:00", "source_system": "github_rest", "source_fetched_at": "2026-10-19T04:35:06.858Z", "github_verified_at": "2026-10-19T04:35:06.858Z", "candidate_eligibility": "eligible", "ineligibility_reasons_json": "[]", "warnings_json": "[]", "newcomer_label_signal": 0, "feature_definition_version": "merged-candidates-v0.4", "normalized_at": "2026-10-19T07:58:20.741790+00:00", "has_reproduction_steps": 0, "has_acceptance_criteria": 0, "has_expected_behavior": 0, "has_affected_module_hint": 0, "task_types_json": "["feature"]", "text_clarity_score": 40.0, "estimated_code_difficulty": 1, "estimated_setup_difficulty": 1, "estimated_project_context_difficulty": 1, "estimated_collaboration_difficulty": 0, "estimated_effort_bucket": "half_day", "novice_fit_probability": 0.417, "newcomer_score": 41.67, "growth_value_score": 35.0, "feature_evidence_json": "{"auxiliary_signals": {"performance": []}, "body_length": 1246, "comment_count": 1, "difficulty_assessment": {"dimensions": {"code": {"confidence": "low", "conflicts": [], "evidence": [], "level": 1, "prior": 1}, "collaboration": {"confidence": "low", "conflicts": [], "evidence": [], "level": 0, "prior": 0}, "project_co