{"key": "preactjs/preact#5325", "repository": "preactjs/preact", "issue_number": 5325, "github_issue_id": "5963965572", "url": "https://github.com/preactjs/preact/issues/5325", "title": "Support custom element registries", "source_files": ["D:\OSS-Mentor\data\teacher_clickhouse\inventory_20261022T172108Z\issues_discovered.json"], "historical_labels": ["feature request"], "beginner_difficulty_confirmed": false, "frozen": false, "decision": "availability_passed", "reason": "current_unassigned_no_observed_claim_or_open_pr", "open_pr_references": [], "claim_signals": [], "current_labels": ["feature request"], "current_signal_group": "historical_signal_only", "body": "A scoped custom element registry can be attached to a document, shadow root, and elements.

When creating elements with `createElementNS`, you need to pass in the custom element registry you want to use, otherwise it defaults to the document's registry:

```js
document.createElementNS(nameSpace, tagName, {
  customElementRegistry,
});
```

If the developer is rendering into a shadow root, Preact will currently create all elements using the document's `customElementRegistry`, rather than the shadow root's.

Some ways around this:

Preact looks up the `customElementRegistry` of the rendered root, and uses that in its calls to `createElementNS`.

Or, an option to `render` allows the developer to provide a `customElementRegistry` when creating elements.

Or, Preact provides a hook to override how `createElementNS` is called.", "language": "JavaScript", "state": "open", "assignees": [], "locked": false, "verified_at": "2026-10-22T17:42:57.860Z", "expires_at": "2026-10-23T17:42:57.860000+00:00", "timeline_complete": true, "bucket": "historical_signal_only"}

