**Prettier 3.9.9**

### Example 1
[Playground link](https://prettier.io/playground/#N4Igxg9gdgLgprEAuEBnA7gSxmAFgAgAoBDASn2HzGNTnwEYl8B6ZqgHSkoCMBufAL6DOIADQgIABxiZoqZKEnEATrWXIQMAJ6S4qMMszSQAgUA)

```sh
--parser typescript
```

**Input:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) { case 1: // c
{ b; } }
```

**Output:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) {
  case 1: { // c
    b;
  }
}
```

**Second Output:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) {
  case 1: {
    // c
    b;
  }
}
```

### Example 2
[Playground link](https://prettier.io/playground/#N4Igxg9gdgLgprEAuEBnA7gSxmAFgAgAoBDASn2HzGNTiOPwGp8AjcgenaoB0okLWAbnwBfUbxAAaEBAAOMTNFTJQs4gCda65CBgBPWXFRh1meSBEigA)

```sh
--parser typescript
```

**Input:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) { case (a + b) // c
: { b; } }
```

**Output:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) {
  case a + b: { // c
    b;
  }
}
```

**Second Output:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) {
  case a + b: {
    // c
    b;
  }
}
```

### Example 3
[Playground link](https://prettier.io/playground/#N4Igxg9gdgLgprEAuEBnA7gSxmAFgAgAoBDASn2HzGNTiOPwGp8AjfAenaoB0pSkKrANz4AvmN4gANCAgAHGJmipkoOcQBOtDchAwAnnLiowGzApCjRQA)

```sh
--parser typescript
```

**Input:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) { case (a + b // c
): { b; } }
```

**Output:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) {
  case a + b: { // c
    b;
  }
}
```

**Second Output:**
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) {
  case a + b: {
    // c
    b;
  }
}
```

### Expected output
<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
switch (a) {
  case 1: {
    // c
    b;
  }
}
```

### Why?

The first format prints the comment after the block's `{`, and the second format moves it to its own line in the block. The output should be stable after the first format. The same happens when the comment is after the test's `)` or last inside its parentheses.

Related: #4428 (a comment before `{` of an `if` block), #12108.

Also reproduces on `main` (88d8e96).

