**Prettier 3.9.10** (also 3.9.9), parser `babel`, default options (`--no-config`).

Formatting a `delete` whose operand carries a JSDoc type cast does not reach a fixed point in one pass: the first pass drops the parentheses, the second pass adds a different pair.

**Input**
```js
function t(window) {
  delete (/** @type {any} */ window).__pwned;
}
```

**Output, pass 1**
```js
function t(window) {
  delete /** @type {any} */ window.__pwned;
}
```

