See comment below https://github.com/prettier/prettier/issues/20307#issuecomment-6244130662


<details>
<summary>Original</summary>



**Prettier 3.9.10** (also 3.9.9), parser `babel`, options `--print-width 100 --single-quote` (no config file).

A two-call member chain whose last argument is an object literal is formatted differently depending on whether the input chain is on one line: the first pass breaks the chain into one call per line, the second pass joins the chain head back onto one line and breaks only the object. The second form is the stable one.

**Input**
```js
async function a(harness, firstPatch) {
  harness.deps.patchDraft.mockReturnValueOnce(firstPatch).mockResolvedValueOnce({ ok: true, status: 200, body: { revision: 20, changed: ['span_a'], plan_name: 'orm' } });
}
```

**Output, pass 1**
```js
async function a(harness, firstPatch) {
  harness.deps.patchDraft
    .mockReturnValueOnce(firstPatch)
    .mockResolvedValueOnce({
      ok: true,
      status: 200,
      body: { revision: 20, changed: ['span_a'], plan_name: 'orm' },
    });
}
```

**Output, pass 2** (formatting pass 1's output; stable from here)
```js
async function a(harness, firstPatch) {
  harness.deps.patchDraft.mockReturnValueOnce(firstPatch).mockResolvedValueOnce({
    ok: true,
    status: 200,
    body: { revision: 20, changed: ['span_a'], plan_name: 'orm' },
  });
}
```

**Expected**: the same output from either input, in one pass. At the default print width of 80 the first pass is already stable, so this needs a width at which the chain head (`harness.deps.patchDraft.mockReturnValueOnce(firstPatch).mockResolvedValueOnce({`) fits on one line.

Reproduce: write the input to `in.mjs`, then
```
npx prettier@3.9.10 --no-config --print-width 100 --single-quote in.mjs > p1.mjs
npx prettier@3.9.10 --no-config --print-width 100 --single-quote p1.mjs > p2.mjs
diff p1.mjs p2.mjs
```


</details>

