body_text:
Dependabot is currently reporting a few vulnerabilities in [`Platforms/emscripten/browser_test/package-lock.json`](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/-/Platforms/emscripten/browser_test/package-lock.json).
These [alerts](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/concepts/supply-chain-security/dependabot-alerts) are separate from the regular updates listed in [`dependabot.yml`](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/.github/dependabot.yml).

There are 5 solutions to this problem:
1. manually update those deps and fix the alerts;
2. manually ask dependabot to create security updates for each alert (like [^1]);
3. manually dismiss the alert;
4. configure Dependabot to check and create PRs to update the deps in `package-lock.json`;
5. configure Dependabot to ignore `package-lock.json` (if possible);

If we decide to go with 1/2/3, we would need to manually intervene for any future alert, so 4/5 are better solutions in the long term.  If we go with 4/5 it should be enough to list the `main` branch in `dependabot.yml` to solve the alerts since Dependabot only looks at the `main` branch, unless we want to update deps on maintenance branches and/or keep all branches aligned.

@hoodmane, do you have any preference?

[^1]: https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/158394

